<title>INDIA: India's IFCI Ltd 1st half 96/97 net up.</title>
<headline>India's IFCI Ltd 1st half 96/97 net up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    1,831.4  vs   1,772.6</p>
<p>    Income from operations   11,332.0  vs   8,117.1</p>
<p>    Other income		     19.2  vs     121.6</p>
<p>    Interest			 8,207.0 vs   5,198.4</p>
<p>  Provision for bad and</p>
<p>    doubtful loans		  227.9  vs     320.4</p>
<p>    Other Expenditure	     433.2  vs     384.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation		    251.7  vs     232.5</p>
<p>    Taxes			     400.0  vs     330.0</p>
<p>NOTE: The Industrial Finance Corporation of India Ltd is one of India's leading term-lenders. The company said the provision for bad and doubtful loans excluded a further provision of 642.3 million rupees (30.9.1995-Nil; previous accounting year ending 31.3.1996 - 500 million rupees) utilised out of special reserve, as permitted by RBI guidelines.</p>
</text>
